          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حتما (ḥatman) is built on the native Arabic root ḥ-t-m, \"to make firm, to decree\" (Lane). Ḥatman is the verbal noun ḥatm, decreeing, with the adverb ending -an: as decreed, inevitably."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
